Mi 4i retained-log ECC: source and real-capture audit, 2026-10-04 UTC

Scope and pins
Offline only; no device access, reboot, flash or new firmware execution. Source pins are pocketboot dcbe3781a3b686a48a7f437051d6738689e8a3e7, Linux 4fecfe9561a33db1320482d5fffb03ce1d8dd7ec, and official lk2nd 23.1 e9c8b21735c13dd7ace808b1e35451638f0a0c6d. Relevant decoder/RS/pstore files are unchanged in the current feature branches. The original raw captures were located in the completed boot session's ignored output, verified against recorded hashes, then copied into private ignored output in the current worktree. Raw captures/logs were not uploaded.

Runtime, not just packaged DT
Both archived clean live logs match the earlier published hashes. Each reports exactly one successful ramoops registration at 0x80000@0x9ff80000 with ecc:64. Neither has a duplicate-probe rejection or lk2nd.pass-ramoops argument. Both image QCDT v2 tables point all three entries to one byte-identical saved FDT containing one ramoops node. The 2x live kernel also logs header-codeword correction counts 23,26,27,21,18,30 at initial probe; those messages have no zone labels.

Static layout check
Linux DT parsing sets only ECC size. ram_core defaults to 128-byte data blocks, 8-bit symbols, polynomial 0x11d, fcr=0, prim=1, matching pocketboot tools/ramoops_rs.c. The separately protected header is 12 bytes. Console size 0x40000 yields capacity174708, 1365 parity slots, data parity at console+0x2aa80, header parity at console+0x3ffc0 (raw+0x7ffc0). An 8192-byte dump record yields capacity5364, data parity+0x1500, header parity+0x1fc0. Decoder allocation, full-block decoding and ring endpoint rules match the kernel. No geometry/codec mismatch was found.

At the lk2nd source pin, lk2nd/ramoops/ramoops.c:56-123 does nothing to the outgoing DT without lk2nd.pass-ramoops. If that option is enabled, it sets ecc-size=0 rather than preserving ECC64. The fixed-size raw staging command at lines125-132 neither invokes that fixup nor interprets ECC. Do not add pass-ramoops to the present ECC64 profile casually.

